  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The city's historic centre has undergone significant changes in recent years. Once a thriving commercial area, it is now largely dominated by souvenir shops and restaurants catering to tourists. This shift has been driven by the increasing number of visitors drawn to the city's famous landmarks and cultural events.\n\nWhile some locals have welcomed the influx of new businesses, others have expressed concerns about the loss of traditional character and the rising costs of living. The city council has introduced measures aimed at promoting local entrepreneurship and preserving the area's heritage, but progress is slow.\n\nAs a result, the historic centre now feels like a place where different worlds coexist – the old and the new, the authentic and the touristy. This blend of cultures can be both fascinating and disorienting for visitors, who must navigate a maze of narrow streets and competing attractions to find the genuine article.\n\nDespite these challenges, the city's historic centre remains one of its most popular destinations, attracting millions of visitors each year. Its unique blend of past and present continues to inspire artists, writers, and musicians, who see it as a vibrant hub of creativity and innovation.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main reason for the shift in the city's historic centre from commercial to tourist-oriented businesses?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The city council's efforts to promote local entrepreneurship\", \"The increasing number of tourists visiting the city's landmarks and cultural events\", \"The rising costs of living for locals\", \"The introduction of new transportation links\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is a common concern among some local residents regarding the changes in the historic centre?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The loss of traditional character and rising costs of living\", \"The influx of new businesses and jobs\", \"The preservation of the area's heritage and promotion of local entrepreneurship\", \"The increase in cultural events and festivals\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is a notable feature of the historic centre?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Its cleanliness and orderliness\", \"Its blend of old and new cultures\", \"Its lack of tourist attractions\", \"Its similarity to other European cities\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the city's cultural scene from the text?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It is dominated by traditional arts and crafts\", \"It is characterized by a mix of old and new influences\", \"It is largely influenced by foreign cultures\", \"It has declined significantly in recent years\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"The author's attitude towards the changes in the historic centre can be described as:\",\n      \"options\": [\"Critical and dismissive\", \"Neutral and observational\", \"Sympathetic and supportive\", \"Ambivalent and nuanced\"],\n      \"answer\": \"option4\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
